    "detailed_description": "Originally released in 1994 for the Commodore Amiga and Amiga CD32 console, this cartoony platformer from Magnetic Fields saw players take on the role of Kid Chaos, a cave-kid captured from prehistory by evil scientists from the future, fighting to escape and find the time machine that can return him home! Now, relive those days in this remastered emulated version.<br><br>Contains both the Amiga and CD32 versions of the game.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Gameplay</h2>As Kid Chaos, you must fight through the evil scientists' artificial environments by causing as much destruction as possible. Jump to swing your club in the air in an arc, or gather up speed and 'whizz' to attack enemies and also reveal secret hidden passages. Use springs to gain speed and ramps to launch yourself into the sky. Each world also features unique bonus levels.<br><br><br>This enhanced version introduces a number of modern features to this retro classic, including:<br><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> Saving/loading the game at any point<br></li><li> Support for most modern game controllers<br></li><li> Full control remapping<br></li><li> Image scaling and smoothing options</li></ul>",
    "about_the_game": "Originally released in 1994 for the Commodore Amiga and Amiga CD32 console, this cartoony platformer from Magnetic Fields saw players take on the role of Kid Chaos, a cave-kid captured from prehistory by evil scientists from the future, fighting to escape and find the time machine that can return him home! Now, relive those days in this remastered emulated version.<br><br>Contains both the Amiga and CD32 versions of the game.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Gameplay</h2>As Kid Chaos, you must fight through the evil scientists' artificial environments by causing as much destruction as possible. Jump to swing your club in the air in an arc, or gather up speed and 'whizz' to attack enemies and also reveal secret hidden passages. Use springs to gain speed and ramps to launch yourself into the sky. Each world also features unique bonus levels.<br><br><br>This enhanced version introduces a number of modern features to this retro classic, including:<br><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li> Saving/loading the game at any point<br></li><li> Support for most modern game controllers<br></li><li> Full control remapping<br></li><li> Image scaling and smoothing options</li></ul>",
    "short_description": "Kid Chaos was kidnapped from prehistory by evil scientists from the future. Fight to escape their artificial environments in this club-swinging, havoc-wreaking, side-scrolling platformer, originally released in 1994 for the Commodore Amiga.",
